        "heading_VxkxVN": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Pressure-Sensitive Labels for Food Processing Applications",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_fmD9mz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Food and beverage processors rely on versatile, cost-effective labels that can withstand transport, moisture, temperature changes, and other harsh conditions—all while capturing consumers’ attention on crowded store shelves. Pressure-sensitive labels (PSLs) meet these demands by offering a durable, attractive solution for branding, product identification, ingredient lists, safety information, and other key messaging.</p><p>Easy to apply yet highly durable, pressure-sensitive labels adhere securely and provide an ideal surface for high-quality printing. Experienced PSL manufacturers can custom-print and die-cut labels in a wide range of sizes, shapes, and materials, allowing brands to achieve a distinctive look that meets their exact specifications. Read on to learn more about the adhesive performance of pressure-sensitive labels and the essential role they play in food processing applications.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-inherit"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_VxkxVN",
        "text_fmD9mz"
      ],
