        "heading_mTfBrQ": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "",
            "heading": "How Do Pressure-Sensitive Labels Work & What Is the Technology Behind Them?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p>Pressure-sensitive labels are the most widely used labeling technology in today’s packaging market. Instead of relying on water-, heat-, or solvent-activated adhesives, PSLs use a pressure-activated adhesive system that bonds to a surface with light to moderate pressure. They can be applied manually or through fully automated pressure-sensitive labeling equipment, making them highly versatile for food and beverage operations.</p><p>A pressure-sensitive label is typically constructed from four key components:</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_GaYMPA": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Release liner",
            "content": "<p>The removable backing that supports the label during storage, handling, and application. It consists of a base liner material and a release coating that prevents the adhesive from adhering until the label is ready to be applied.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_qUjbKh": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Adhesive",
            "content": "<p>The pressure-activated adhesive layer that enables the label to bond securely to packaging materials, containers, or processing equipment surfaces.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_ycGUCY": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Facestock",
            "content": "<p>The primary material that carries the printed graphics, branding, ingredient statements, barcodes, and other required information.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_Rz6gxE": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Topcoat",
            "content": "<p>A protective coating or laminate applied to the facestock to enhance print quality, resist moisture or abrasion, and deliver the desired finish.</p><p>The release liner plays a critical role in ease of use. Because it is engineered with low-surface-energy materials—such as siliconized paper or film—it allows the adhesive to separate cleanly from the liner when pressure is applied to the facestock during application. This controlled release ensures consistent dispensing and reliable adhesion across a wide range of food processing surfaces and packaging formats.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
