        "heading_F3fPr3": {
          "type": "heading",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "",
            "heading": "What Are the Key Benefits of Using Pressure-Sensitive Labels?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p>Pressure-sensitive labels are the most widely used labeling technology in today’s packaging market. Instead of relying on water-, heat-, or solvent-activated adhesives, PSLs use a pressure-activated adhesive system that bonds to a surface with light to moderate pressure. They can be applied manually or through fully automated pressure-sensitive labeling equipment, making them highly versatile for food and beverage operations.</p><p>A pressure-sensitive label is typically constructed from four key components:</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_yQBKKa": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Are the Key Benefits of Using Pressure-Sensitive Labels?",
            "content": "<p>Pressure-sensitive labels are cost-effective and simple to apply—either manually or with automated equipment. They are designed to withstand demanding environments involving friction, abrasion, sterilization processes, moisture, humidity, UV exposure, and other extreme conditions. Their pressure-activated adhesive enables reliable bonding on humid, rough, dusty, or lightly contaminated surfaces, as well as on challenging substrates such as rubber and non-polar polyolefin materials.</p><p>PSLs are also an environmentally friendly labeling option, as many constructions minimize the use of volatile compounds and incorporate recyclable or disposable components.</p><p>Another major advantage is customization. Pressure-sensitive labels are compatible with high-definition printing technologies, allowing for extensive flexibility in size, shape, materials, colors, finishes, and functional design features. This versatility makes them ideal for meeting diverse branding, regulatory, and product identification needs in food processing applications.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": true,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_H4Ej76": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Applications Do Pressure-Sensitive Labels Serve in Food Processing Applications?",
            "content": "<p>The durability, ease of application, and versatility of pressure-sensitive labels make them ideal for a wide range of food and beverage processing needs. PSLs are used throughout the industry to identify, brand, and provide regulatory information for countless types of consumable goods. Common applications include:</p><ul><li><strong>Candies and confectionery products</strong></li><li><strong>Canned and jarred foods</strong></li><li><strong>Condiments, dressings, and spreads</strong></li><li><strong>Frozen and refrigerated foods</strong></li><li><strong>Jams, jellies, and preserves</strong></li><li><strong>Sauces, marinades, and syrups</strong></li><li><strong>Spices, seasonings, and dry mixes</strong></li><li><strong>Specialty beverages, craft drinks, and alcoholic beverages</strong></li></ul><p>These examples represent only a portion of the food products that rely on pressure-sensitive labels for clear, durable, and compliant packaging identification.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_FmtWHX": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Pressure-Sensitive Labeling Solutions From NADCO",
            "content": "<p>Industries such as food and beverage processing depend on pressure-sensitive labels to meet branding, compliance, and product identification requirements. These labels must perform reliably across a wide range of packaging formats and production environments.</p><p>At <strong>NADCO® Tapes & Labels, LLC</strong>, we produce both standard and fully customized pressure-sensitive labels tailored to each customer’s specifications. Our capabilities include flexographic printing, spot color printing, and short-run digital printing in up to seven colors, along with in-house prototyping, die-cutting, slitting, and converting. These integrated services allow us to deliver precise, high-quality labels that align with your brand and operational needs.</p><p>All NADCO® products are manufactured in the USA using advanced equipment and high-performance materials to ensure consistent results, fast lead times, and dependable quality.</p><p><a href=\"https://info.nadco-inc.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Contact us</strong></a> to learn more about our pressure-sensitive label solutions or <a href=\"/pages/request-a-quote\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Request a Quote\"><strong>request a quote</strong></a> to get started on your next project.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
